course: dictionary
lesson: 15388
title: Spectator
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A spectator is a person who watches something happen without taking part. The clues are in the sentence: «The spectators cheered when the goal went in.» They cheered, so they were watching the match, but they were not the ones playing.
explain: Try swapping in your meaning to check it. «The spectators sat in the stands while the players ran on the pitch.» The players are taking part, and the spectators are watching, so a spectator is someone who watches, not someone who plays.
explain: Spectators also appear in maths. «There were 3,450 spectators at the match.» You can round this number to the nearest thousand, which gives 3,000, because 3,450 is closer to 3,000 than to 4,000.
fact: A spectator is a person who watches an event without taking part.
fact: Spectators often go to sports matches, shows and concerts.
fact: «Spectator sport» means a sport that many people like to watch.
fact: «Spectator» is a noun: one spectator, many spectators.
fact: In maths, numbers of spectators can be added, compared and rounded.
exercise: What is a spectator? | A referee who blows the whistle | A person who sells the tickets | *A person who watches an event without taking part | A player who scores the goals
exercise: «The spectators cheered loudly when the goal went in.» Who cheered? | The goalkeeper | The players on the pitch | The referee | *The people watching the match
exercise: «There were 3,450 spectators.» Round 3,450 to the nearest thousand. | *3,000 | 3,500 | 3,400 | 4,000
test: «A spectator sport is one that many people like to watch.» What does spectator sport mean? | A sport only for children | A sport with no players | A sport played with no rules | *A sport that many people like to watch
test: Which person is a spectator? | *A fan sitting in the stand watching the match | A football player running on the pitch | A bus driver taking fans to the match | The coach giving team talks
exam: «The spectators watched the magic show from their seats.» What does spectators mean in this sentence? | People who perform on stage | Tickets for the show | Magicians | *People who watch without taking part
